  "title": "IMUMIA2026: Multi-paradigm motor-imagery EEG dataset (IMU-MI_A)",
  "description": "A multi-paradigm motor-imagery EEG dataset recorded from healthy participants at Inner Mongolia University. It covers five body-part tasks (hand, foot, thumb, index finger, index-thumb pinch) with left/right laterality, performed under a Classic Arrow paradigm and a Cue-Execution dual-stage paradigm. This BIDS release is a public five-subject sample of a 244-participant dataset, recorded with a 64-channel Neuroscan system at 1000 Hz.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a Neuroscan SynAmps amplifier and a 64-channel Quik-Cap (Ag/AgCl passive electrodes, 1000 Hz, Cz reference, forehead ground, impedance below 10 kOhm), plus EOG, ECG and EMG channels. Each participant completed one session of five runs, one motor-imagery task per run. Visual arrow cues were presented, followed by 4 s of imagery.",
